Handling time matters most for option C, so here is how sensitive it is.

data sens = handling time,mean wait,longest wait; 20 min (today),32.8,51; 15 min,14.6,34; 12 min,5.8,19
chart bar sens y=mean wait,longest wait unit=min title="Pre-registered fast lane: wait by handling time"

## Truck by truck

Wait in minutes for each arrival. Appointments are left out here because the wait just becomes the schedule shift, which equals the baseline column.

data replay = arrival,haulier,log,baseline,second operator,pre-registered,gate screen; 06:12,O'Brien Haulage,4,0,0,0,0; 06:20,Kowalczyk & Sons,11,12,0,4,12; 06:31,D'Angelo Farms,19,21,1,5,21; 06:44,"Prairie Rose Co-op (Bin 7, east side)",27,28,0,4,28; 06:52,Nguyen Bros,31,40,0,8,2
data replay += 07:05,"Halvorsen Grain, Ltd.",38,47,0,7,27; 07:09,M. Okonkwo,44,51,3,15,43; 07:23,O'Brien Haulage,41,49,1,13,37; 07:38,"Sunderland & Pike (contract: “Fall Spot”)",52,42,0,10,34; 07:41,Kowalczyk & Sons,49,51,3,19,39
